colon-subdirs (1.1.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * COLON_WRAP default is built-in rewrite; COLON_WRAP=1 uses PATH stem;
    COLON_WRAP=<name> execs that binary.
  * Document full command options in --help and man pages (no need to consult
    the original tool manuals for common flags).
  * Add shell integration tests under tests/shell/ that create fixtures, run
    each colon-* command, and assert results (wired into Meson).
  * Fix rewrite mode exit status after fork (run_exec_wait / run_exec_pair)
    so :rm leaf pruning and similar post-exec steps see the real status.
  * Treat leading colon-paths (:foo/bar) as BASE "/" (same as /:foo/bar).
  * For :mv/:cp destinations, substitute the first ':' with '/' safely.
  * Add built-in rewrite backends under src/rewrite/ for each wrapped command.
  * Update README and unit tests for empty-left paths and COLON_WRAP.

 -- Lenik (谢继雷) <lenik@bodz.net>  Mon, 20 Jul 2026 13:15:00 +0800

colon-subdirs (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: colon-path wrappers for mv, cp, zip, rm, rmdir, scp,
    unzip, and rsync. Each command is built standalone (no shared library).
    Installs :cmd symlinks to colon-cmd binaries.

 -- Lenik (谢继雷) <lenik@bodz.net>  Fri, 17 Jul 2026 01:00:00 +0800
